        {
          "id": 1701997638,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Yeah, I think the ability to do that might have been added as part of the same \"fit into Windows networks better\" work that the \"check group membership with upcalls\" I mentioned in your recent bug as part of.  (The ACL support was part of that work as well, which is why the ACLs are more like Windows/NFSv4 ACLs than like POSIX ACLs, the references to the POSIX.1e draft in the man pages notwithstanding.)",
